icance (referenced in 122 Wikipedia editions). Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The Great Pyramid of Giza, constructed around 2559 BCE, stands as the largest and oldest of the three pyramids in the Giza necropolis, located near Cairo, Egypt. This architectural marvel was commissioned by Pharaoh Khufu, also known as Cheops, and is a defining symbol of ancient Egyptian civilization, representing the apex of pyramid construction techniques. It holds immense significance as one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, drawing millions of visitors and scholars interested in its engineering and cultural implications.

